  "text": "Grandma shared her own account after learning why her friends had stayed away.\n\nYou helped arrange today’s gathering, Pip. Would you like to welcome everyone?\n\nM129 45q-10 0-10 12v42q0 12 13 12h12l-7 15 31-15h60q13 0 13-12V57q0-12-13-12Z\n\nThe empty seed boat stays at its mooring. The seed remains where you left it.\n\nThe boy steps onto the dock with the same repaired bird. The tape stays here.\n\nYou choose the position. Sol uses his ladder and tools; Pip waits beside him.\n\nWord help isn't available for this word right now. Your writing is unchanged.\n\nGrandma opens the storage beside her bench and brings out the spare cushions.\n\nA flat piece of baked clay or similar material used to cover a roof or floor.\n\nTell Grandma what Sol wants to share. Sol will keep his page in his satchel.\n\nPip takes the remaining repair rope. The other rope stays where you left it.\n\nLights held in protective coverings; here, flowers that keep story pictures.\n\nSol brought his manuscript to the garden. Mara remained at work at the dock.\n\nRina gave permission. Guide Pip to the shelf and take the intact spare tile.\n\nRina checked the flour sacks after the roof repair. The flour was still dry.\n\nThe cracked tile is set aside. Choose where Sol should place the spare tile.\n\nAnother window has newer progress. Load it before making more saved changes.\n\nThe repair box is empty. Both ropes are already in use or in Pip’s backpack.\n\nThe last boat returns. Its operator brings it alongside the passenger dock.\n\nSol shared the original draft of A Small Repair with its ending still open.\n\nMara is still working. Grandma wants her to have the story she just shared.\n\nThe parts of plants that produce seeds; here, the garden’s lantern flowers.\n\nA particular spot or position. Here, stays in place means it does not move.",
  "textSha256": "bb28ad85ddc5ca250244320023b782d9aca692cacf26b9ab8034e7d0878534fd",
